<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LanguageData>

  <!-- Settings: window category (mod-list entry) -->
  <!-- EN: Unique Melee Weapons -->
  <UMW_SettingsCategory>ユニークな近接武器</UMW_SettingsCategory>

  <!-- Settings: section headers. -->
  <!-- EN: Weapons -->
  <UMW_SettingsWeapons>武器</UMW_SettingsWeapons>

  <!-- EN: Generation -->
  <UMW_SettingsGeneration>生成</UMW_SettingsGeneration>

  <!-- EN: Traders -->
  <UMW_SettingsTraders>商人</UMW_SettingsTraders>

  <!-- EN: Compatibility -->
  <UMW_SettingsCompat>互換性</UMW_SettingsCompat>

  <!-- Settings: reusable label suffixes. Each includes a leading space, and every applicable one is
       appended (no precedence between them), so they must read cleanly back to back. -->
  <!-- EN:  (default) -->
  <UMW_DefaultSuffix>(デフォルト)</UMW_DefaultSuffix>

  <!-- {0} is another piece of content the current value matches, named from its own def label. -->
  <!-- EN:  (same as {0}) -->
  <UMW_SameAsSuffix>(「{0}」と同じ)</UMW_SameAsSuffix>

  <!-- Settings: Weapons. One checkbox per weapon. {0} is the weapon's own def label (lowercase). -->
  <!-- EN: Allow {0} to be generated. Turn off to remove it from every reward and loot pool; the other weapons fill its place. Weapons already in your save are untouched. Some mods' own loot generators may bypass this. -->
  <UMW_WeaponEnabledDesc>「{0}」の生成を許可します.オフにすると全ての報酬プールと戦利品プールから除外され,他の武器がその枠を埋めます.セーブデータに既に存在するものはそのまま残ります.MODによっては独自の戦利品生成処理でこの設定が無視される場合があります.</UMW_WeaponEnabledDesc>

  <!-- Settings: buttons -->
  <!-- EN: Reset to defaults -->
  <UMW_ResetToDefaults>デフォルトに戻す</UMW_ResetToDefaults>

  <!-- Settings: Generation -->
  <!-- {0} is the wood resource's item label (ThingDef WoodLog, "wood" in English, lowercase). -->
  <!-- EN: Exclude {0} from generated unique weapons -->
  <UMW_ExcludeWoodStuff>生成されるユニークな武器から「{0}」を除外する</UMW_ExcludeWoodStuff>

  <!-- {0} is the vanilla longsword's item label (lowercase), named as the example reward. -->
  <!-- EN: Unique weapons roll a random eligible material. With this on, wood is never rolled, so a hard-won reward never lands as a wooden {0}. -->
  <UMW_ExcludeWoodStuffDesc>ユニークな武器は,条件を満たす材料の中から無作為に抽選されます.オンにすると木材が抽選から除外されるため,苦労して手に入れた報酬が木製の「{0}」になることはありません.</UMW_ExcludeWoodStuffDesc>

  <!-- Shown only when Royalty is active; the traits it governs need that DLC.
       {0}, {1}, {2} are the three trait labels (lowercase): monomolecular, plasma-cored, zeus-headed. -->
  <!-- EN: Allow ultratech weapon traits -->
  <UMW_AllowUltratechTraits>最先端の技術力による武器特性を許可する</UMW_AllowUltratechTraits>

  <!-- EN: Three traits use Royalty's ultratech kit: {0}, {1} and {2}. Turn off to keep them out of the roll, for medieval or low-tech runs. Other traits are unaffected; weapons that already rolled one keep it. -->
  <UMW_AllowUltratechTraitsDesc>3つの特性はRoyaltyの最先端技術級の装備を使用します:「{0}」,「{1}」,「{2}」.オフにするとこれらは抽選に加わりません.中世限定や低技術レベルでのプレイを想定した設定です.他の特性には影響せず,既に引いている武器はその特性を保持します.</UMW_AllowUltratechTraitsDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Traders. Both toggles default off. The row label is a shared template: {0} is the
       trader kind's own def label ("武器屋", "呪い商" per Core's own translation); each description's
       {0} is the same label. -->
  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in {0} stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniques>「{0}」の在庫にユニークな武器を含める</UMW_TraderStocksUniques>
  <!-- EN: About half of {0} visits bring one unique melee weapon for sale, and the caravan buys unique melee weapons either way. Ultratech traits never roll on its stock: a war party deals in period arms. Disabled weapons never appear. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesWarMerchantDesc>「{0}」の来訪のうち約半数で,ユニークな近接武器が1つ販売品として並びます.また,在庫の有無に関わらずユニークな近接武器を買い取ります.その在庫に最先端技術級の武器特性が乗ることはありません:襲撃団はその時代の武具を扱っているためです.「武器」の項でオフにした武器は登場しません.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesWarMerchantDesc>
  <!-- EN: About half of {0} visits bring one unique melee weapon for sale, and the caravan buys unique melee weapons either way. Ultratech traits may roll on its stock: shamans trade in relics they do not fully understand. Disabled weapons never appear. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShamanDesc>「{0}」の来訪のうち約半数で,ユニークな近接武器が1つ販売品として並びます.また,在庫の有無に関わらずユニークな近接武器を買い取ります.その在庫には最先端技術級の武器特性が乗ることもあります:呪い商は自分でも仕組みを理解しきれていない遺物を扱っています.「武器」の項でオフにした武器は登場しません.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShamanDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Abilities. Slider labels are shared templates: {0} is the subject's own def label
       (an ability, a hediff, or the warband faction), capitalized; {1} is the slider's current value.
       The unit word is part of the template, so hour- and day-based cooldowns are separate keys. -->
  <!-- EN: {0} cooldown: {1} hours -->
  <UMW_AbilityCooldownHours>「{0}」のクールダウン: {1}時間</UMW_AbilityCooldownHours>

  <!-- EN: {0} cooldown: {1} days -->
  <UMW_AbilityCooldownDays>「{0}」のクールダウン: {1}日</UMW_AbilityCooldownDays>

  <!-- EN: {0} radius: {1} cells -->
  <UMW_AbilityRadius>「{0}」の半径: {1}セル</UMW_AbilityRadius>

  <!-- EN: {0} duration: {1} hours -->
  <UMW_HediffDurationHours>「{0}」の持続時間: {1}時間</UMW_HediffDurationHours>

  <!-- EN: Rest time between earthshakes. The default matches Odyssey's EMP pulser. 0 removes the cooldown. -->
  <UMW_EarthshakeCooldownDesc>地響きを起こしてから次に起こせるようになるまでの間隔です.初期値はOdysseyの「EMPパルサー」に合わせてあります.0に設定するとクールダウンはなくなります.</UMW_EarthshakeCooldownDesc>

  <!-- EN: Reach of the stunning shockwave. Walls do not stop it; gaps with no floor do. It is indiscriminate: a wider radius catches your own colonists too. -->
  <UMW_EarthshakeRadiusDesc>スタンさせる衝撃波が届く範囲です.壁では止まりませんが,床のない隙間は越えられません.この衝撃は敵味方を区別しないため,半径を広げるほど自分の入植者も巻き込まれます.</UMW_EarthshakeRadiusDesc>

  <!-- EN: Rest time between rallying cries. Measured in days on purpose: the default makes it an heirloom moment, not a standing aura re-applied every fight. -->
  <UMW_RallyingCryCooldownDesc>鼓舞の叫びを上げてから次に上げられるようになるまでの間隔です.時間ではなく日単位にしてあるのは意図的なもので,初期値では戦闘ごとに掛け直す常設のオーラではなく,家宝にふさわしい特別な瞬間になります.</UMW_RallyingCryCooldownDesc>

  <!-- EN: How far the cry carries. Rallies every non-hostile humanlike in range with line of sight; blocked by walls. Also wakes sleepers. -->
  <UMW_RallyingCryRadiusDesc>叫びが届く範囲です.この範囲内で使用者に敵対しておらず,かつ視線が通っている人型は全て鼓舞されます.壁に遮られます.眠っている者も目を覚まさせます.</UMW_RallyingCryRadiusDesc>

  <!-- EN: How long the rallied buff lasts, halving pain and stagger time. Sleepers are woken instead, and resent it. -->
  <UMW_RalliedDurationDesc>士気高揚の効果が続く時間です.効果中は痛みとよろめきの時間が半分になります.眠っていた者は鼓舞されるかわりに叩き起こされ,それを不快に思います.</UMW_RalliedDurationDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Quests. The slider label reuses the shared template pattern: {0} is the warband
       faction's def label (capitalized), {1} the value. The desc's quest examples (ancient
       mercenaries, bandit camps, item stashes) are vanilla content names; translate them to match
       the official localization. -->
  <!-- EN: {0} quest commonality: {1} -->
  <UMW_QuestWeight>「{0}」クエストの出現頻度: {1}</UMW_QuestWeight>

  <!-- EN: How often the warband quest is offered against the other opportunity-site quests (ancient mercenaries, bandit camps, item stashes...). Higher = offered more often. 0 disables it. -->
  <UMW_WarbandQuestWeightDesc>他の同種の地点クエスト(古代の傭兵,盗賊の野営地,埋蔵品...)に対する,戦士団クエストの出現頻度です.高くするほど提示されやすくなります.0にするとこのクエストは無効になります.</UMW_WarbandQuestWeightDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Compatibility. Shown only when Vanilla Textures Expanded is active. The toggle
       defaults on and is read when the game loads, hence the restart sentence. {0} is our unique
       spear's def label (lowercase); {1} is that mod's display name from its About.xml, injected so
       neither is restated here. Deliberately says nothing about performance. -->
  <!-- EN: Match the {0} to {1} -->
  <UMW_MatchVteSpear>{0}を{1}に合わせる</UMW_MatchVteSpear>

  <!-- EN: {1} draws the vanilla spear diagonally and longer. With this on, the {0} is turned and enlarged to match it in a drafted pawn's hands. Purely cosmetic. Takes effect after a restart. -->
  <UMW_MatchVteSpearDesc>{1}はバニラのスピアを斜めに,かつ元より長く描きます.この設定がオンの場合,{0}も同様に向きと大きさが変更され,臨戦状態の入植者の手の中で合わせられます.見た目だけの変更で,再起動後に反映されます.</UMW_MatchVteSpearDesc>

</LanguageData>
